WEBVTT

00:00:20.745 --> 00:00:24.707
After centuries as a delivery boy,
nothing surprises me.

00:00:29.378 --> 00:00:30.796
You stink, loser.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:31.922
Hey, Fry!

00:00:32.006 --> 00:00:34.550
Pizza going out! Come on!

00:00:34.925 --> 00:00:37.845
All right. I'll take the Red Rocket.

00:00:49.065 --> 00:00:53.903
Hello! Pizza delivery for D. Frosted Wang.

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:56.322
Not another crank delivery!

00:00:56.405 --> 00:00:58.324
Why don't I read these things
ahead of time?

00:01:00.768 --> 00:01:01.936
One time was funny.

00:01:02.019 --> 00:01:04.355
But every week for 10 years? Not as funny.

00:01:04.605 --> 00:01:07.483
True, not as funny.
But, still, somewhat funny.

00:01:11.028 --> 00:01:13.823
And then they burst out laughing
a second time.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:20.872
I've been a delivery boy
for a thousand years.

00:01:20.997 --> 00:01:23.374
Isn't there any room
for promotion around here?

00:01:23.457 --> 00:01:25.835
There'll be no promotions
unless somebody dies.

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:27.003
And even then,

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.088
only if we can't bring them back
as a zombie, like Scruffy.

00:01:30.339 --> 00:01:33.050
Life and death are a seamless continuum.

00:01:33.509 --> 00:01:35.761
Well, could I at least get
some encouragement?

00:01:35.845 --> 00:01:37.513
I could use a shot in the arm.

00:01:38.806 --> 00:01:40.057
I got shot in the leg!

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:44.187
Roberto! What are you doing here?

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.606
What? A fella can't drop in on old friends

00:01:46.689 --> 00:01:48.482
and hold them hostage?

00:01:48.566 --> 00:01:50.359
I'm good. And you?

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.362
Attention,
criminal robot in the building!

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.906
Come out with your hands up!

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:57.575
- Never!
- Other guy.

00:01:57.658 --> 00:02:00.453
Listen up, piggies, I want a hovercopter,

00:02:00.736 --> 00:02:02.363
and an unmarked sandwich,

00:02:02.446 --> 00:02:05.783
and a new face with,
like, a Hugh Grant look.

00:02:05.866 --> 00:02:07.910
And every five minutes I don't get it,

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:10.788
someone's going to get stabbed in the ass!

00:02:10.871 --> 00:02:12.164
He's bluffing.

00:02:12.248 --> 00:02:13.916
Ouch! He's not bluffing!

00:02:15.493 --> 00:02:17.036
You call for a chopper?

00:02:17.119 --> 00:02:20.289
No, I specifically said hovercopter!

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.874
One chopper coming up.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.584
Hiya!

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:28.005
All right! Way to go.

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:32.843
You know, URL,

00:02:32.927 --> 00:02:34.970
sometimes it's almost too much for me.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.722
You mean, the respect we get?

00:02:36.806 --> 00:02:39.642
And the high level of job satisfaction?

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:41.394
There's that, but I'm also talking about

00:02:41.477 --> 00:02:43.688
the non-stop promotions
and the free hot rod.

00:02:48.025 --> 00:02:50.319
I do love a man in uniform.

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:55.074
I mean, a uniform
that doesn't involve short pants.

00:02:56.575 --> 00:02:58.536
I can see I have no future here.

00:02:58.619 --> 00:03:01.372
My only option is to resign with dignity.

00:03:01.455 --> 00:03:03.165
Here are my shorts.

00:03:11.132 --> 00:03:13.592
Hello. I'd like to enroll
in Police Academy.

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:15.386
You think you can just waltz in here

00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:17.138
with no pants and become a cop?

00:03:17.221 --> 00:03:19.056
-That's the plan.
-I like you, kid.

00:03:19.223 --> 00:03:20.433
I got no pants on, either.

00:03:20.516 --> 00:03:22.685
I can see that.
You're quite a bit taller than me.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:25.104
Welcome to Police Academy.

00:03:25.187 --> 00:03:26.564
Hi, I'm Fry.

00:03:26.647 --> 00:03:28.607
I'm the Sound Effects 5000.

00:03:34.822 --> 00:03:37.783
Wow. That would be impressive
if you were a human.

00:03:37.867 --> 00:03:39.118
Yeah.

00:03:39.201 --> 00:03:40.896
On your feet for Chief O'Manahan.

00:03:41.005 --> 00:03:42.008
At ease, cadets.

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:45.624
I'll make this short and sweet,
'cause I'm PMSing like a lumberjack.

00:03:45.708 --> 00:03:47.710
Police Academy is not for everybody.

00:03:47.877 --> 00:03:49.837
You're gonna get your boob scuffed.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.048
But if you've got the vulva
to stick it out,

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:54.842
I'll be proud to call you ladies
"policemen."

00:03:54.925 --> 00:03:56.177
Sir! Yes, ma'am!

00:04:04.018 --> 00:04:05.353
Yeah. That's great.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.646
Now, can you actually turn on
the ignition?

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:09.648
I don't have any hands.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.628
Well,
it's that time of the month.

00:04:30.753 --> 00:04:32.463
Graduation day.

00:04:32.546 --> 00:04:36.050
So grow a pair and put them together
for our new officers!

00:04:39.595 --> 00:04:41.263
Hooray for the pigs!

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:44.141
Graduates, you are hereby officially cops.

00:04:44.266 --> 00:04:46.268
Now move it along, nothing to see here.

00:04:51.107 --> 00:04:53.526
Hooray! Free sky sticks!

00:04:54.819 --> 00:04:56.612
Police brutality!

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.581
Nice. All right.

00:05:07.665 --> 00:05:10.209
Before we head out,
I'll be teaming up our new officers

00:05:10.292 --> 00:05:12.044
with their ironically matched partners.

00:05:12.128 --> 00:05:13.587
Sound Effects 5000,

00:05:13.671 --> 00:05:14.964
you'll be with Cranski.

00:05:16.799 --> 00:05:18.092
Ow! My tinnitus!

00:05:18.175 --> 00:05:21.554
Fry, due to the unfortunate loss
of Officer Smith,

00:05:21.637 --> 00:05:23.097
you'll be riding with URL.

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:26.559
And Smitty was just
a few days from retirement.

00:05:26.642 --> 00:05:27.634
What happened?

00:05:27.712 --> 00:05:30.688
He took a early retirement. Damn.

00:05:33.758 --> 00:05:35.593
Let's get down to business.

00:05:35.676 --> 00:05:38.638
Aren't you going to say,
"Good news, everyone"?

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:41.474
Oh, I just said that for Fry's benefit.

00:05:41.557 --> 00:05:44.977
Made the poor fellow feel better
about his pointless job.

00:05:45.061 --> 00:05:46.646
As much as I miss him,

00:05:46.729 --> 00:05:48.648
he didn't really serve
much purpose around here.

00:05:48.731 --> 00:05:50.816
Though he did walk Zoidberg.

00:05:52.235 --> 00:05:54.862
In any case, I've improved on Fry

00:05:54.946 --> 00:05:57.073
by sticking some wheels on a board,

00:05:57.156 --> 00:06:01.160
so Leela and Bender can easily make
the next delivery without him.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.995
Neat. So, where we going?

00:06:03.746 --> 00:06:04.997
Pandora.

00:06:05.081 --> 00:06:06.791
That dangerous 3D planet?

00:06:06.916 --> 00:06:08.584
Can't we just send our avatars?

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:11.462
No, it's cheaper just to have you die.

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:19.428
Whoa!

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:21.556
Fifteen miles over the speed of light.

00:06:21.639 --> 00:06:25.142
That's a violation of the law
of Lorentz invariance, baby.

00:06:25.226 --> 00:06:26.227
Light 'em up.

00:06:48.124 --> 00:06:50.334
Look out for that particular individual!

00:06:52.253 --> 00:06:54.005
An electric wall, eh?

00:06:54.088 --> 00:06:57.174
I can't see the harm in peeing on that.

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:11.814
Whoa! Where'd my man learn that?

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:14.025
Sunny D commercial.

00:07:16.861 --> 00:07:18.905
Let's refract this sucker.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:41.135
DNA and career chip, please.

00:07:42.845 --> 00:07:44.722
Erwin Schrödinger, huh?

00:07:44.805 --> 00:07:46.891
What's in the box, Schrödinger?

00:07:46.974 --> 00:07:50.728
A cat, some poison and a cesium atom.

00:07:50.811 --> 00:07:52.521
The cat, is it alive or dead?

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:55.233
-Alive or dead?
-Answer him, fool.

00:07:55.399 --> 00:07:57.902
It's a superposition of both states

00:07:57.985 --> 00:08:00.196
until you open it
and collapse the wave function.

00:08:00.363 --> 00:08:01.697
Says you.

00:08:05.201 --> 00:08:07.787
There's also a lot of drugs in there.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:20.258
So, you're a robot?

00:08:28.766 --> 00:08:30.351
You boys did good.

00:08:30.434 --> 00:08:32.770
Nailed a major violator
of the laws of physics.

00:08:32.937 --> 00:08:36.107
He's going down. Cat's gonna testify.

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:38.776
Guys like this really bust my uterus.

00:08:38.859 --> 00:08:40.444
You're both getting a promotion.

00:08:40.528 --> 00:08:42.405
Ever heard of the Future Crimes Division?

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:43.948
Tomorrow, I have.

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:57.587
Oops.

00:08:58.629 --> 00:09:00.089
I can't make out a thing.

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:02.967
Well, I guess you
should have had two eyes.

00:09:03.092 --> 00:09:05.720
Just deliver the package,
and let's get out of here.

00:09:05.803 --> 00:09:08.097
Screw that! I ain't no delivery boy.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.932
I'm the company chef.

00:09:10.099 --> 00:09:12.435
Oh, you're the chef, are you?

00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:14.896
Then why don't you make us
something nice to eat?

00:09:15.563 --> 00:09:18.065
I'll make you something nice...

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:22.445
Here's your damn peanut butter
and jelly sandwich!

00:09:28.659 --> 00:09:31.704
Now that we can predict crimes
with 99% accuracy,

00:09:31.787 --> 00:09:35.041
we can arrest most perpetrators
before they even perpetrate anything.

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:38.502
That's ridiculous.
Only horoscopes can predict the future.

00:09:38.586 --> 00:09:40.046
That's what we used to think.

00:09:40.129 --> 00:09:42.381
Until we invented this.

00:09:47.887 --> 00:09:49.263
Oh!

00:09:49.347 --> 00:09:50.765
Slow down, baby.

00:09:50.848 --> 00:09:54.518
The Cybernetic Oracle.
The ultimate man-machine hybrid.

00:09:54.602 --> 00:09:56.687
Programmed with every crime ever recorded,

00:09:56.771 --> 00:10:00.233
and implanted with the brain cells
of history's greatest detectives.

00:10:00.316 --> 00:10:02.026
We call him Pickles.

00:10:02.235 --> 00:10:04.528
On account of it's like
he's floating in a jar?

00:10:04.612 --> 00:10:06.030
Exactly.

00:10:06.155 --> 00:10:09.116
The Oracle's visions are recorded
on these colored balls.

00:10:09.367 --> 00:10:11.702
Green is larceny. Black is fraud.

00:10:11.786 --> 00:10:13.788
Red, homicide.

00:10:14.038 --> 00:10:16.499
-What's pink polka-dots?
-Clown slaughter.

00:10:16.582 --> 00:10:18.626
It happens more often than you'd think.

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:22.380
Floater in the bowl!

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.632
Red ball. Homicide!

00:10:24.715 --> 00:10:25.716
Woo!

00:10:27.718 --> 00:10:29.136
Suspect, male, 6'1".

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:31.097
Distinctive mustard stain on his forehead.

00:10:33.391 --> 00:10:34.684
My kajigger!

00:10:34.767 --> 00:10:36.519
Victim, Hattie McDoogal.

00:10:41.983 --> 00:10:43.651
Look, the clock says 5:08.

00:10:43.818 --> 00:10:45.319
It's 4:30 right now.

00:10:45.528 --> 00:10:49.323
Uh-oh. We only have a half hour
to chill out before we head over.

00:10:52.535 --> 00:10:53.995
Oh, Hattie.

00:10:54.078 --> 00:10:59.000
When I look into your one good eye,
I see a reflection of beauty.

00:10:59.083 --> 00:11:01.335
Oh! Fresh.

00:11:01.419 --> 00:11:02.878
Freeze, fool.

00:11:02.962 --> 00:11:04.672
You're under arrest for future murder!

00:11:04.755 --> 00:11:05.798
Yeah?

00:11:05.881 --> 00:11:09.844
You can't arrest me for future murder
after it's right now murder!

00:11:09.927 --> 00:11:11.178
My kajigger!

00:11:18.102 --> 00:11:20.521
So, he didn't really want to marry me?

00:11:20.605 --> 00:11:25.192
No. See, he knew you left everything
to your parakeets in your will.

00:11:25.276 --> 00:11:27.695
He was going to murder you,
marry your parakeets,

00:11:27.778 --> 00:11:30.615
and then poison them
with an arsenic-laced cuttlebone.

00:11:30.781 --> 00:11:33.868
Classic move. Aw, yeah.

00:11:36.245 --> 00:11:39.290
-Congratulations on your big bust.
-You, too.

00:11:39.373 --> 00:11:41.584
Keep it up, and you boys
might just make detective.

00:11:41.667 --> 00:11:42.752
Now, if you'll excuse me,

00:11:42.835 --> 00:11:44.337
I got to go drop a big one.

00:11:44.962 --> 00:11:47.089
Wow. I can't believe it.

00:11:47.256 --> 00:11:50.009
One more promotion,
and I'll be a real detective,

00:11:50.092 --> 00:11:52.803
like Sherlock Holmes or Speed Buggy.

00:11:54.722 --> 00:11:57.099
Eight pounds. I'm naming her Burt.

00:11:57.183 --> 00:12:00.811
Mazel tov, Chief.
That's a beautiful bathroom baby.

00:12:03.898 --> 00:12:05.483
Ain't you heading home, Phil?

00:12:05.566 --> 00:12:08.319
In a minute.
I just want to finish this paperless work.

00:12:08.402 --> 00:12:10.029
Don't stay up too late.

00:12:10.112 --> 00:12:12.865
We got a lot of people to shoot tomorrow.

00:12:17.703 --> 00:12:20.081
Hello! Anyone?

00:12:20.331 --> 00:12:22.750
There's never a cop around
when you need one.

00:12:24.293 --> 00:12:26.379
Green ball. Larceny.

00:12:36.847 --> 00:12:39.934
Hmm. The thief seems to be
some sort of ghost.

00:12:40.017 --> 00:12:41.644
Or is he?

00:12:45.022 --> 00:12:46.440
Bender?

00:12:55.449 --> 00:13:00.246
Item seven, our corporate tax rate
remained unchanged this fiscal year.

00:13:00.329 --> 00:13:01.455
That's not funny.

00:13:01.539 --> 00:13:04.041
It's not supposed to be funny.
It's a business meeting.

00:13:04.125 --> 00:13:06.127
Things used to be funny around here.

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:09.005
Noses were picked, pants fell down.

00:13:09.088 --> 00:13:10.423
So, what changed?

00:13:10.506 --> 00:13:13.384
Only Fry could say, and he's gone.

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:17.096
Hey. Bender and Leela
are back from Pandora.

00:13:17.179 --> 00:13:18.389
-How was it?
-Awful.

00:13:18.472 --> 00:13:20.308
We had nothing to say to each other,

00:13:20.391 --> 00:13:23.519
so we had to listen to Bender's
Eagles album for 27 hours.

00:13:23.644 --> 00:13:25.938
Beats talking to you, witchy woman.

00:13:26.022 --> 00:13:27.899
Hey, he's back!

00:13:27.982 --> 00:13:29.609
- Look at you.
- Hubba hubba.

00:13:29.692 --> 00:13:32.278
Your pants go almost
all the way to your ankles.

00:13:32.361 --> 00:13:33.988
Good afternoon, individuals.

00:13:34.071 --> 00:13:35.907
Sir, would you mind
stepping out of the building?

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:38.034
Normally, when a cop asks me that,

00:13:38.117 --> 00:13:40.411
I spray whipped cream
in his eyes and run away,

00:13:40.494 --> 00:13:42.747
but to ditch these losers, gladly.

00:13:44.624 --> 00:13:46.042
Bender, be honest with me.

00:13:46.125 --> 00:13:47.668
Are you planning a big heist?

00:13:47.752 --> 00:13:49.503
Usually, but not at the moment.

00:13:49.587 --> 00:13:51.964
I only ask 'cause the Oracle thinks
you're going to pull off

00:13:52.048 --> 00:13:53.925
a major theft next Thursday.

00:13:54.216 --> 00:13:56.177
Next Thursday, you say?

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:57.845
Pray, continue.

00:13:58.095 --> 00:14:01.182
Are you familiar
with this particular location?

00:14:01.265 --> 00:14:03.893
I may have a burgling familiarity with it.

00:14:03.976 --> 00:14:06.854
Does the word "Maltese"
mean anything to you?

00:14:06.938 --> 00:14:09.106
The Maltese Liquor, the strongest

00:14:09.190 --> 00:14:11.525
and most valuable malt liquor ever brewed!

00:14:11.609 --> 00:14:14.487
And soon it will be mine.

00:14:15.821 --> 00:14:17.240
I'm sorry. You were saying?

00:14:17.365 --> 00:14:20.660
Bender, I'm only telling you this
so you can avoid committing the crime.

00:14:21.077 --> 00:14:24.330
"Avoid committing the crime." Got it.

00:14:24.789 --> 00:14:26.791
You wrote "Commit the crime!"

00:14:32.672 --> 00:14:35.258
Oh, there's got to be
some way to stop Bender.

00:14:35.341 --> 00:14:36.926
Maybe something in the Oracle's prediction

00:14:37.009 --> 00:14:39.220
that I missed before, due to incompetence.

00:14:41.889 --> 00:14:43.891
Wait. Who's the trigger-happy jerk?

00:14:49.146 --> 00:14:51.524
That's me! I recognize the face.

00:14:53.985 --> 00:14:56.696
You shot me! You miserable dingus!

00:14:57.572 --> 00:15:00.283
No! No! What have I will have done?

00:15:00.366 --> 00:15:03.703
Man, that's heavy. Osmium heavy.

00:15:03.786 --> 00:15:06.080
Are you going to turn me in
for concealing evidence?

00:15:06.163 --> 00:15:08.874
Say what? You're my partner, home Fry.

00:15:08.958 --> 00:15:11.377
Besides, I got my own secrets.

00:15:12.378 --> 00:15:14.088
Anything big worth checking out?

00:15:14.171 --> 00:15:17.425
Just your big jangly booty, baby.

00:15:17.508 --> 00:15:19.385
See you tonight, toots.

00:15:21.846 --> 00:15:24.015
You and the chief?

00:15:24.265 --> 00:15:26.350
Mmm-hmm. We been getting it on.

00:15:26.517 --> 00:15:28.311
Right there in your chair.

00:15:28.394 --> 00:15:31.105
I'm like, "Oh, baby! Oh, baby!"

00:15:31.397 --> 00:15:35.443
And she's like, "Yeah. Yeah. Yeah."

00:15:40.823 --> 00:15:43.075
I would never shoot Bender. Never!

00:15:43.159 --> 00:15:44.702
He taught me how to shave.

00:15:46.996 --> 00:15:48.456
Revision ball.

00:15:48.539 --> 00:15:52.543
By deciding not to shoot Bender,
you created an alternate future.

00:15:53.669 --> 00:15:57.381
I could never shoot you. Never!
You taught me how to shave.

00:15:57.465 --> 00:15:58.591
See?

00:15:58.674 --> 00:16:00.885
Just get out of here. Go!

00:16:02.595 --> 00:16:05.139
Now, dig the unintended consequences.

00:16:05.306 --> 00:16:10.686
My friends, let us share this booze
in a toast to our dear friend, Bender.

00:16:20.112 --> 00:16:21.155
Oops.

00:16:21.239 --> 00:16:24.533
The Maltese Liquor
done destroyed their brains.

00:16:24.617 --> 00:16:26.369
Fools should have known it's fatal

00:16:26.452 --> 00:16:29.080
for anyone but robots
and Billy Dee Williams.

00:16:29.914 --> 00:16:33.417
So, if I don't shoot Bender
all my other friends will die?

00:16:33.542 --> 00:16:36.879
Fate is a freaky mistress.
Much like the chief.

00:16:36.963 --> 00:16:38.005
Look out!

00:16:38.089 --> 00:16:40.549
Something's not right.
I refuse to believe it.

00:16:40.633 --> 00:16:42.051
Rewind.

00:16:50.977 --> 00:16:52.061
Ooh!

00:16:52.144 --> 00:16:54.730
Are you the calloused
working man I ordered?

00:16:54.855 --> 00:16:56.357
Uh... Sure.

00:16:57.358 --> 00:16:59.360
In order to fix your leaky roof,

00:16:59.443 --> 00:17:02.738
I'll need to spend two or three hours
down here in the wine cellar.

00:17:02.822 --> 00:17:05.825
I'll be upstairs
putting batteries in things.

00:17:09.036 --> 00:17:10.121
Whoa!

00:17:10.913 --> 00:17:12.540
The Maltese Liquor.

00:17:12.623 --> 00:17:14.500
Forty ounces of heaven!

00:17:17.253 --> 00:17:19.505
Here, boy. This is for you.

00:17:20.798 --> 00:17:23.134
Ahh!

00:17:23.885 --> 00:17:24.969
Hmm...

00:17:31.434 --> 00:17:33.394
Invisible safe, eh?

00:17:40.735 --> 00:17:42.236
Oh, yeah, baby!

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.113
210 proof.

00:17:44.196 --> 00:17:45.948
That's all the proof I need.

00:17:47.408 --> 00:17:48.492
Put the bottle back.

00:17:48.659 --> 00:17:50.536
We both know I won't do that.

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:52.038
Either you're going to shoot me,

00:17:52.121 --> 00:17:53.956
or I'm going to spray
whipped cream in your eyes

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:55.625
and walk out of here like a big shot.

00:17:55.708 --> 00:17:56.751
Bender, no!

00:17:56.834 --> 00:17:59.211
You don't have to do something
just 'cause it's going to happen.

00:17:59.295 --> 00:18:01.589
The future's making a chump out of you.

00:18:01.672 --> 00:18:04.884
Oh, yeah? Well, I'm going to make
a chump out of the future.

00:18:04.967 --> 00:18:06.469
I'm not stealing anything!

00:18:06.844 --> 00:18:09.597
Yes! I stopped the crime
without shooting you.

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:11.599
The Oracle was wrong.

00:18:11.682 --> 00:18:12.850
Was I?

00:18:14.477 --> 00:18:15.978
-Pickles?
-Yes.

00:18:16.062 --> 00:18:17.688
It is I, Pickles.

00:18:17.772 --> 00:18:19.273
I set the whole thing up.

00:18:19.357 --> 00:18:23.861
Everyone will think Bender's the thief
while I make off with that glorious brew.

00:18:24.237 --> 00:18:25.821
Seriously? Why?

00:18:25.905 --> 00:18:28.449
So I can kill my human brain cells.

00:18:28.658 --> 00:18:30.910
Do you have any idea what a burden it is

00:18:30.993 --> 00:18:33.246
to know everything that will ever happen?

00:18:33.329 --> 00:18:34.956
To never be surprised.

00:18:35.039 --> 00:18:38.584
To know the punch line
of every joke hours in advance.

00:18:38.751 --> 00:18:39.877
Like watching Leno.

00:18:40.002 --> 00:18:43.381
And that is why I faked
the prediction of this crime.

00:18:43.673 --> 00:18:45.967
Nevertheless, stay with me here,

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:49.554
things will now happen
just as I fake predicted.

00:18:49.762 --> 00:18:52.723
Bender, you're going
to hand me that bottle.

00:18:53.349 --> 00:18:54.559
Not that one!

00:18:54.642 --> 00:18:58.229
The real one, which you switched
when Fry stupidly looked away.

00:18:58.312 --> 00:18:59.397
Hey.

00:18:59.522 --> 00:19:02.233
Oh, man. Why you got to be so Oracle-y?

00:19:03.359 --> 00:19:06.070
Fry, you are going to shoot Bender,

00:19:06.153 --> 00:19:08.489
killing him and shattering
the fake bottle,

00:19:08.573 --> 00:19:10.825
just as I predicted.

00:19:10.908 --> 00:19:12.577
Do it! It is your destiny!

00:19:12.785 --> 00:19:14.829
Funny thing about destiny.

00:19:15.037 --> 00:19:17.582
Sometimes fate has other plans.

00:19:18.249 --> 00:19:19.584
Oh!

00:19:20.418 --> 00:19:21.502
Oh, nuts.

00:19:21.586 --> 00:19:22.712
You shot me!

00:19:22.795 --> 00:19:24.755
You miserable dingus!

00:19:25.047 --> 00:19:27.925
And now the part I didn't show you.

00:19:28.551 --> 00:19:29.635
Oh!

00:19:30.011 --> 00:19:32.221
Everyone will think Bender killed you,

00:19:32.555 --> 00:19:35.057
and I walk away with the goofy juice!

00:19:37.727 --> 00:19:39.687
Ah! Ah!

00:19:39.896 --> 00:19:42.607
Finally, blissful ignorance.

00:19:42.690 --> 00:19:45.359
I have no idea
what's going to happen next.

00:19:45.443 --> 00:19:47.612
Did you get that, Chief?

00:19:51.115 --> 00:19:54.201
We got it all from behind
this prediction-proof glass.

00:19:54.452 --> 00:19:57.705
But how could you know
my prediction was fake?

00:19:57.955 --> 00:20:01.000
I knew something was wrong,
but I couldn't put my finger on it.

00:20:01.083 --> 00:20:02.627
Then, it hit me.

00:20:03.336 --> 00:20:04.629
You showed Bender

00:20:04.712 --> 00:20:07.340
sharing the deadly booze with our friends.

00:20:07.423 --> 00:20:08.883
Bender would never share.

00:20:08.966 --> 00:20:10.218
The very idea!

00:20:10.301 --> 00:20:12.553
So we set up this little charade

00:20:12.637 --> 00:20:15.556
based on an episode of Speed Buggy.

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:17.975
With the added benefit of me and the chief

00:20:18.059 --> 00:20:20.478
being locked in a small room.

00:20:23.314 --> 00:20:26.067
Shall we adjourn to the dungeon?

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:32.406
Well, I got my shield for stopping Bender.

00:20:32.657 --> 00:20:34.575
Way to go, Fry!

00:20:34.742 --> 00:20:36.994
But, then I got fired
for tipping off Bender.

00:20:38.871 --> 00:20:42.375
Fry, we have no idea
what you do around here,

00:20:42.458 --> 00:20:44.335
but we desperately need you back.

00:20:44.543 --> 00:20:45.670
Really?

00:20:45.753 --> 00:20:49.131
Um, I don't suppose there's any chance
I could get a promotion.

00:20:49.257 --> 00:20:50.967
Sure. What the heck?

00:20:51.092 --> 00:20:53.427
I hereby promote you to

00:20:53.553 --> 00:20:56.055
executive delivery boy.

00:20:56.305 --> 00:20:57.473
Executive?

00:20:57.682 --> 00:20:59.141
It's a meaningless title.

00:20:59.225 --> 00:21:02.687
But it helps insecure people
feel better about themselves.

00:21:03.563 --> 00:21:05.690
I feel better about myself!